  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a positive integer NNN. In one operation you can:\n\n\nEither subtract 333 or subtract 444 from NNN.\nCan you make NNN zero by performing any number of operations?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe only line of each test case contains a positive integer NNN, denoting the integer which you need to make zero.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output `YES` if you can make NNN zero using any number of operations. Otherwise, print `NO`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `YES`, `yEs`, `yes`, and `yeS` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1041 \\leq N \\leq 10^41≤N≤104"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n3\n7",
        "output": "NO\nYES\nYES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: You cannot make N=1N=1N=1 zero by performing any number of operations.\nTest case 222: Subtract 333 from N=3N=3N=3 to make it zero in one operation.\nTest case 333: Subtract 444 from N=7N=7N=7 to make it N=3N=3N=3 in one operation. Then, subtract 333 from N=3N=3N=3 to make it zero in second operation."
      }
    ]
  },
